WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:05.040
(glass breaking)
(rock music playing)

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.200
- [Vin] I remember saying, c'mon,

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.380
Dom can't just lift up this car.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.140
I've seen people look
at me like I was crazy,

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.100
like of course you can.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:21.340
It's technically possible.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.680
If anyone can do it, it's Dom.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.600
And I'm thinking, oh my god,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.940
the belief that you all have
in Dom is just profound.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:32.840
It was so enticing because it
was so much wish fulfillment.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.560
God, we were asked to fly.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:36.120
- Dom, cars don't fly.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.940
- [Vin] And it was that
moment where we realized,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.400
Fast and Furious didn't need
to be restricted in any way.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.160
We were allowed these outrageous moments

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.660
and flying through the air
from building to building

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:50.620
was playing to that.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.080
It was one of those answers to the riddle,

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.540
how do we one up the
spectacle of each film.

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.360
Traditionally, we always tried to take

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.860
a practical approach first.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.080
The first film, we went to
race car driving school.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.180
As we continued making a film,

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.160
it was more important for us
to go to stunt driving school.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.820
So we'll take practical run.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.900
But something as outrageous as that, ah.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.220
If you wanna know if Paul
and I drove from one building

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.720
to the next, as much as
I'd like to say, maybe,

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.640
it's pretty obvious that might
not have been the smartest

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:23.560
thing for us to do.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.840
What's funny is if you
talk to us back then,

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.520
we'd be willing to do anything.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.380
Without taking away the
magic of movie making,

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:36.120
thank god that that was in 2014
and we were able to use CGI

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.040
the way we did.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.660
And you can learn as much as you want

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.120
when it's actually shoot day,

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.220
and the pyrotechnics are
launching fireballs in the air

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.680
and you're driving through smoke,

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.460
it's always a dangerous thing.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.140
I don't think the world
realized how much risk

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.960
one has to consider when doing

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.460
some of those action sequences with cars.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.860
Fortunately, we were safe.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.080
It's been so many great stunts,

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:01.440
I say this is in the top five.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.220
My first reaction was giddy.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.020
I was like holy shit, we pulled it off.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:06.940
(Vin laughing)

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.600
I was kinda blown away.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.940
When you're sitting in that
theater and you see that scene,

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.900
the first thing that reacts
is the inner child in you

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.960
and that's a testament
to an iconic moment.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.880
After the first film, Paul
Walker and I were at the airport

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.780
and we're just sitting on the floor,

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.700
people were walking over us

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.700
and he looked over at me
and said take all this in

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.680
because this will be our
last moment of anonymity.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.140
He knew that we struck a
chord in the public somehow.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.000
It's a big part of my life.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.940
Both the happy times and
the severe melancholy

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.620
that has come with this whole franchise.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.120
But I'm proud of every
moment and every frame

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:50.600
and everybody that's contributed

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.500
to this record breaking saga.

